Further Information:
When u.uhunger is between 1500 and 2000, lesshungry sets nomovemsg
to "You're finally finished" before asking you whether to stop
eating or not.  If you say yes, it clears it to NULL, but if you say
no, it leaves it.  However, if stop_occupation gets called for an
unrelated reason before you finish your meal, nomovemsg does not get
cleared.  For the message to be printed, however, unmul() would need
to be called without changing nomovemsg and without supplying a
msg_override.  There are only three places where unmul() is called
without a msg_override: one is in steal.c, when a nymph tries to
steal worn armor.  The second is in the once-per-turn section of
allmain.c, when multi reaches zero (so, to trigger the bug, multi
would have to be set negative without changing nomovemsg), and the
third is in vault.c, which I did not investigate.


